    CF-186 was filed minutes ago by the sibling code-factory-pm lane (dd547d7) and its
    AC4 froze a plan sentence — `plus two lettered sub-arms, §4b and §7b` — that the
    tree has not carried since CF-183 landed at 5069c0a. At aef18d2 the plan says
    `plus three lettered sub-arms, §4b, §7b and §31b`, so an implementer following
    AC4 would compare against a phrase that does not exist and could also try to
    delete a §7c that is already gone. AC4 now names the lettered arms the tree
    actually carries (§4b, §7b, §31b) and reads the count from the plan's own sentence
    in its `plus N lettered sub-arms, …` shape, with the current value quoted and the
    post-AC1 value (four) stated, so the criterion stays falsifiable across the fix.
    
    Nothing else about the row changed: it remains P3, pending, with its probe field
    intact — re-running the row's own probe at this tip still prints
    `lettered=3 cf155_rows=0 suite=PASS` (exit 0), which is AC0's pre-fix state. No
    row count moved: the sibling had already taken the file to 163 rows (CF-188 and
    CF-189 landed while this tick was measuring), and this commit changes one existing
    row (CF-186: `acceptance_criteria`, `foreman_note`, `updated_at`) and appends one
    event.
    
    Event 326 (`audit`, task CF-182) records this tick: the lane, the measured tip
    aef18d2 (161 rows / 322 events at measurement), the CF-183 closure that moved out
    of the milestone exclusion list, the duplicate disclosure against dd547d7, and the
    three gate readings.
    
    Conflict resolution, disclosed: the rebase over 4edeba4 conflicted in both board
    files. Every sibling line is preserved byte-for-byte; the only replaced line is
    the sibling's stale copy of CF-186 (same id, same title, pre-AC4 text), and this
    tick's audit event was renumbered 323 -> 326 past the sibling maximum (325). Read
    back after the merge: 163 task rows, 326 events, 0 duplicate ids in either file,
    every line parses with `jq -c .`, no conflict markers.
    
