s that the documented lifecycle state of destroy is contradicted by the shipped script.", "acceptance_criteria": "0. Reproduce: with CRIER_URL and BUNKER_SERVER set and no node inference key, run the documented create; the failure path prints `cleanup required: bunker destroy <agent> --server <server>`, and running that line destroys the agent (rc=0, archive-then-delete, SSH key removed) as measured above.\n1. Document and script agree: either docs/OPERATIONS.md §8 records destroy as a MEASURED step (naming the run, the date, the archive-before-delete behaviour and the ~435 MB home it archived), or scripts/node-create.sh stops printing a command the runbook forbids. Renew, rebuild and full teardown may stay BLOCKED, but they are separated from destroy instead of sharing its verdict.\n2. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` and `scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK` at the fix commit.", "probe": "grep -n 'cleanup required' scripts/node-create.sh; grep -n 'BLOCKED / NOT YET\\|not a guessed command' docs/OPERATIONS.md | head -4; echo 'measured 2026-11-04: bunker destroy node-myrepo-042342 --server bunker-mvp -> rc=0, \"Agent node-myrepo-042342 destroyed.\", home 435.2 MB archived'", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:28:59Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:28:59Z"}
